---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import SiteLayout from "../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import { pageSeo } from "../../seo/registry.mjs";
import cover from "../../assets/scrum-mastering-1/guidebook-cover.png";
import badge from "../../assets/scrum-mastering-1/rsm1-badge.png";
const chapters = ["Scrum in a Nutshell", "The Scrum Team", "The Team's Scrum Master", "Modes of the Scrum Master", "People Outside the Team", "The Team Swarm", "Leadership", "The Backlog", "Technical Debt", "The Story's Definition of Done", "Velocity, Size, and Effort", "Backlog Refinement", "Planning Day", "The Daily Scrum", "Scaling an Organization"];
const clusters = [chapters.slice(0, 4), chapters.slice(4, 8), chapters.slice(8, 12), chapters.slice(12)];
const progression = [
 ["Study", "Learn each chapter's official objectives with the agent tutor."],
 ["Apply", "Connect the material to your own work and domain experience."],
 ["Check", "Take an official objective-based check."],
 ["Unlock", "Score at least 80% to unlock the next chapter."],
 ["Earn RSM1", "Complete all requirements within 12 months to earn RSM1."],
];
---
<SiteLayout metadata={pageSeo["/training/scrum-mastering-1"]}>
<main id="main" class="sm1-page">
 <section class="sm1-hero">
  <div class="shell">
   <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><ol><li><a href="/">3Back</a></li><li><a href="/training">Training</a></li><li aria-current="page">Scrum Mastering I</li></ol></nav>
   <div class="hero-grid">
    <div class="hero-title"><p class="eyebrow">Scrum Leadership Series</p><h1>Scrum Mastering I: Facilitating Improvement</h1><p class="hero-heading">Learn to lead the improvement game.</p></div>
    <div class="hero-cover"><Image src={cover} alt="Cover of Scrum Mastering I: Facilitating Improvement by Dan Rawsthorne and Doug Shimp." width={300} widths={[180, 300, 450, 600]} sizes="(max-width: 600px) 112px, (max-width: 900px) 220px, 300px" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" /></div>
    <div class="hero-body"><p>Scrum gives a team a way to organize around complex work. SM1 shows you how a Scrum Master helps that team make decisions, confront impediments, protect accountability, and continuously improve how the work gets done.</p><p>Study at your own pace with an agent tutor grounded in the SM1 guidebook. Apply each idea to your own work and demonstrate your understanding of the learning objectives chapter by chapter. Complete the requirements to earn the <a href="https://scrumguide.org/recognized-courses/scrum-master-1/">Recognized Scrum Master 1</a> (RSM1) credential, recognized by the Scrum Guide Organization and verifiable at ScrumGuide.org.</p></div>
    <div class="hero-offer"><p class="offer-line">$150 | Printed guidebook included | 12 months to complete</p><button class="enrollment" type="button" disabled>Enrollment coming soon</button><p class="shipping"><a href="/policies">Printed-book delivery is limited to available destinations. Additional shipping charges may apply.</a></p></div>
   </div>
  </div>
 </section>
 <div class="proof-strip"><ul class="shell"><li>15 chapters</li><li>80% to advance</li><li>12 months</li><li>RSM1 credential</li></ul></div>
<section class="sm1-section section-rule"><div class="shell split"><h2>Go beyond running Scrum events</h2><div class="section-body"><p>A Scrum Master does more than schedule meetings and repeat framework rules. SM1 develops a practical account of the role from inside the Team: how authority works, how decisions are made, how improvement is facilitated, and how the Team stays accountable for its work.</p>
<p>Through the course, you will learn to:</p>
<ul><li>Distinguish the responsibilities of the Team Member, Product Owner, Scrum Master, Business Owner, Stakeholder, and Subject Matter Expert</li><li>Facilitate Team decisions, Retrospectives, and Intraspectives</li><li>Organize work through the Team Swarm</li><li>Protect Product Owner priority decisions and Team accountability</li><li>Expose Technical Debt and strengthen the Definition of Done</li><li>Improve refinement, planning, daily adaptation, and organizational scaling decisions</li></ul></div></div></section>
<section class="sm1-section section-rule"><div class="shell split"><h2>Learn the Scrum Mastering I model</h2><div class="section-body"><p>This is not a generic summary of the 2020 Scrum Guide. SM1 teaches the positions developed in Scrum Mastering I: Facilitating Improvement and identifies where those positions differ.</p>
<p>You will examine the Team Swarm, seven Team Values, Agreement-Based Planning, the Team Captain, Abnormal Termination, the book&#x27;s treatment of Technical Debt, and the distinction between Acceptance Criteria and Standard of Care.</p></div></div></section>
<section class="sm1-section section-rule"><div class="shell"><h2>Demonstrate what you understand</h2><p>Work through the 15 chapters in sequence.</p><ol class="progression">{progression.map(([title, copy], index) => <li><span class="step-number" aria-hidden="true">{String(index + 1).padStart(2, "0")}</span><h3>{title}</h3><p>{copy}</p></li>)}</ol><p>When an answer reveals a gap, the tutor returns to the missed objectives before you try again.</p></div></section>
<section class="credential-band"><div class="shell credential-grid"><Image src={badge} alt="Recognized Scrum Master 1 credential badge." width={138} height={135} loading="lazy" /><div><h2>Recognition based on demonstrated understanding, not attendance alone</h2><p>Earn RSM1 by completing all 15 chapters and passing the required objective-based checks within 12 months. The credential recognizes demonstrated understanding of the Scrum Mastering I learning objectives. Domain experience is where that understanding is put to work.</p>
<p>Your RSM1 credential is recognized by the Scrum Guide Organization and verifiable at ScrumGuide.org.</p></div></div></section>
<section class="sm1-section section-rule"><div class="shell split"><h2>What your $150 includes</h2><div class="section-body"><ul><li>Twelve months of access to the complete self-paced SM1 course</li><li>An agent tutor grounded in the SM1 guidebook</li><li>Official objective-based knowledge checks</li><li>A printed copy of Scrum Mastering I: Facilitating Improvement</li><li>The <a href="https://scrumguide.org/recognized-courses/scrum-master-1/">Recognized Scrum Master 1</a> credential</li><li>Recognition and verification through ScrumGuide.org</li></ul>
<p>The public self-paced course does not include a live instructor or office hours.</p></div></div></section>
<section class="sm1-section section-rule"><div class="shell"><h2>Fifteen chapters. One complete course.</h2><div class="curriculum">{clusters.map((cluster, index) => <ol start={index * 4 + 1}>{cluster.map(chapter => <li>{chapter}</li>)}</ol>)}</div></div></section>
<section class="sm1-section section-rule"><div class="shell split"><h2>Put it to work in your domain</h2><div class="section-body"><p>The course can teach the material and test your understanding. It cannot supply your domain experience for you. The value comes from recognizing how these ideas appear in the work you are already doing and deciding how to apply them there.</p></div></div></section>
<section class="sm1-section section-rule"><div class="shell split"><h2>Ready to begin?</h2><div class="section-body"><p>Build a stronger working understanding of the Scrum Master role and earn recognition for demonstrating it.</p><p class="offer-line">$150 | Complete within 12 months</p><button class="enrollment" type="button" disabled>Enrollment coming soon</button></div></div></section>
<section class="closing-band"><div class="shell split"><h2>Looking for a deeper path?</h2><div class="section-body"><p>Private Live and Domain Guide courses are available as part of the Domain Guides program.</p><a class="domain-link" href="/domain-guides">Explore the Domain Guides program</a></div></div></section>
</main>
</SiteLayout>
<style>
.sm1-page { overflow-wrap: break-word; }
.sm1-hero { padding: 26px 0 44px; }
.breadcrumb { margin-bottom: 24px; font-size: .875rem; }
.breadcrumb ol { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px 16px; list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; }
.breadcrumb li + li::before { content: "/"; margin-right: 16px; color: var(--slate); }
.hero-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) 300px; column-gap: 68px; align-items: start; }
.hero-title { grid-column: 1; }
.eyebrow { margin-bottom: 10px; color: var(--amber-text); font-weight: 700; font-size: .875rem; letter-spacing: .08em; text-transform: uppercase; }
h1 { font-size: clamp(2.25rem, 3.8vw, 3.35rem); line-height: 1.12; margin-bottom: 14px; }
.hero-heading { font-size: 1.6rem; font-weight: 600; line-height: 1.2; margin-bottom: 20px; }
.hero-cover { grid-column: 2; grid-row: 1 / 4; align-self: center; }
.hero-cover img { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; box-shadow: 0 12px 24px rgb(29 36 33 / 12%); }
.hero-body { grid-column: 1; }
.hero-body p { margin-bottom: 16px; font-size: 1.0625rem; line-height: 1.5; }
.hero-offer { grid-column: 1; }
.offer-line { margin: 6px 0 14px; font-size: 1.125rem; font-weight: 700; }
.enrollment { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; min-height: 48px; padding: 11px 22px; border: 1px solid var(--slate); background: transparent; color: var(--charcoal); opacity: 1; font-weight: 700; cursor: default; }
.shipping { max-width: 630px; margin: 12px 0 0; font-size: .875rem; line-height: 1.45; }
a { text-underline-offset: 3px; }
.proof-strip { border-block: 1px solid var(--rule); }
.proof-strip ul { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr); list-style: none; padding-block: 21px; padding-left: 0; margin-block: 0; }
.proof-strip li { font-weight: 700; text-align: center; border-right: 1px solid var(--rule); }
.proof-strip li:last-child { border: 0; }
.sm1-section { padding: 78px 0; }
h2 { font-size: clamp(1.9rem, 3vw, 2.65rem); }
.split { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, .85fr) minmax(0, 1.15fr); gap: 80px; }
.section-body p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
.section-body ul { padding-left: 22px; margin-block: 22px; }
.section-body li { margin-bottom: 12px; }
.progression { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(5, minmax(0, 1fr)); list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 32px 0; border-top: 3px solid var(--amber); }
.progression li { padding: 22px 20px 10px 0; margin-right: 20px; border-right: 1px solid var(--rule); }
.progression li:last-child { border: 0; margin-right: 0; }
.step-number { display: block; color: var(--amber-text); font-size: .875rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 18px; }
.progression h3 { font-size: 1.375rem; }
.progression p { line-height: 1.5; }
.credential-band { padding: 70px 0; background: var(--charcoal); color: var(--paper); }
.credential-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 138px minmax(0, 820px); gap: 64px; align-items: center; }
.credential-grid img { width: 138px; height: auto; }
.credential-grid h2 { max-width: 760px; }
.credential-grid p:last-child { margin: 0; }
.curriculum { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 32px; }
.curriculum ol { margin: 12px 0 0; padding: 18px 0 0 24px; border-top: 1px solid var(--slate); }
.curriculum li { margin: 0 0 14px; padding-left: 4px; }
.curriculum li::marker { color: var(--amber-text); font-weight: 600; }
.closing-band { padding: 60px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); }
.domain-link { display: inline-block; margin-top: 14px; font-weight: 700; text-decoration-thickness: 2px; }
.domain-link:hover { color: var(--amber-text); }
@media (max-width: 900px) {
 .hero-grid { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) 220px; gap: 0 30px; }
 .split { gap: 36px; }
 .curriculum { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
 .progression { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
 .progression li { margin: 0; padding: 18px 0; border-right: 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); }
 .step-number { float: left; margin: 3px 20px 0 0; }
 .progression p { margin-bottom: 0; }
 .credential-grid { gap: 30px; }
}
@media (max-width: 600px) {
 .sm1-hero { padding: 18px 0 28px; }
 .breadcrumb { margin-bottom: 22px; }
 .breadcrumb ol { gap: 5px 8px; }
 .breadcrumb li + li::before { margin-right: 8px; }
 .hero-grid { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) 112px; column-gap: 14px; }
 .hero-title { grid-column: 1 / -1; }
 h1 { font-size: 2.1rem; margin-bottom: 12px; }
 .hero-heading { font-size: 1.3rem; margin-bottom: 20px; }
 .hero-cover { grid-column: 2; grid-row: 2; align-self: start; }
 .hero-offer { grid-row: 2; }
 .hero-offer .offer-line { margin-top: 0; font-size: 1rem; }
 .hero-offer .enrollment { padding: 10px 8px; }
 .hero-body { grid-column: 1 / -1; grid-row: 3; margin-top: 24px; }
 .enrollment { width: 100%; }
 .proof-strip ul { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); gap: 14px 0; }
 .proof-strip li:nth-child(2) { border: 0; }
 .sm1-section { padding: 48px 0; }
 .split, .credential-grid, .curriculum { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 16px; }
 .split h2 { margin-bottom: 8px; }
 .credential-band { padding: 48px 0; }
 .credential-grid img { margin-bottom: 14px; }
 .closing-band { padding: 44px 0; }
}
</style>
